# Hook Patterns

## Return Type

❌ BAD - returning array, no types:
function useAuth() {
  return [user, setUser, loading, error, signIn, signOut];
}
const [user, setUser, loading, error, signIn, signOut] = useAuth(); // confusing

✅ GOOD - return named object with types:
interface UseAuthReturn {
  user: User | null;
  isLoading: boolean;
  signIn: (provider: Provider) => Promise<void>;
}
function useAuth(): UseAuthReturn {
  return { user, isLoading, signIn };
}

## Functions in Hooks

❌ BAD - unstable function reference:
function useAuth() {
  const signIn = async () => { ... }; // new function every render
  return { signIn };
}

✅ GOOD - memoized with useCallback:
function useAuth() {
  const signIn = useCallback(async () => { ... }, []);
  return { signIn };
}

## Logic in Components

❌ BAD - business logic in component:
function AuthScreen() {
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false);
  const [error, setError] = useState(null);
  const signIn = async () => {
    setLoading(true);
    try { await api.signIn(); }
    catch (e) { setError(e); }
    finally { setLoading(false); }
  };
}

✅ GOOD - extract to hook:
function AuthScreen() {
  const { signIn, isLoading, error } = useAuthFlow();
}
